network: 10 % of messages lost, 5 % of delivered messages duplicated

1 increments + retry (at-least-once)     intended 100  replicas:  113  118  113   WRONG and replicas DIVERGE
    a lost ack causes a resend of an increment that was already applied
2 increments + retry + op-id dedup       intended 100  replicas:  100  100  100   CORRECT
    each replica remembers op ids it applied: a resend changes nothing
3 read, add 1, write the value back      intended 200  replicas:  164  164  164   WRONG (but replicas agree)
    two clients raced 36 times; each race lost one update
4 G-counter, before the final exchange   intended 200  replicas:  200  198  197   WRONG and replicas DIVERGE
    replicas lag behind each other while messages are lost: not yet converged
4 G-counter, after anti-entropy          intended 200  replicas:  200  200  200   CORRECT
    converged after 5 more exchanges

(primary-backup rows show the one surviving copy, the promoted backup)
5 primary-backup, asynchronous           intended 100  replicas:   94   WRONG
    6 increments were acknowledged to the client but had not reached the backup when the primary crashed
6 primary-backup, synchronous            intended 100  replicas:  101   WRONG
    op 71 was applied at the backup, its ack was lost in the crash, and the client's resend applied it again
7 primary-backup, synchronous + dedup    intended 100  replicas:  100   CORRECT
    the resend of op 71 is recognised by its op id: every acknowledged increment survives, none counts twice
